<%# The device frame's MEDIA DOCK — every design CTA the card's panel carries
    (Change animation, Add design / Change media, Header background,
    Reposition, Mobile background), stood OUTSIDE the phone.

    Inside the frame those pills float over the bottom of the screen the
    creator is trying to look at: "I want all CTAs for editing outside of the
    phone for the mobile editor, this gives the user more space to see the
    mobile". The rail on the card's other side already does this for Card N,
    Why, Duplicate and Delete; this is the same idea for the panel's own
    controls, on the other side.

    PROXIES, not copies. Each button here names the real pill by selector
    (data-proxy) and device-frame#proxy clicks it, so the handler that runs is
    the one the panel's pill has always run — the same media-picker method,
    the same closest(".survey-card-wrap") — and there is no second set of
    wiring to drift. Which proxies SHOW is also the real pills' decision:
    application.css keys each one on the wrap :has()-ing its original, so a
    branch that renders no Change animation shows no Change animation here,
    and a Reposition the picker hides ([hidden]) disappears here with it.
    Only in the device frames (.device-mobile / .device-tablet, see the
    stylesheet); the desktop editor never draws it. %>
<div class="card-media-dock" role="group" aria-label="<%= t("editor.design", default: "Design") %>">
  <button type="button" class="dock-btn dock-animation"
          data-proxy=".add-animation-fab"
          data-action="click->device-frame#proxy"
          title="<%= t("editor.change_animation_title", default: "Change this card's animation") %>">
    <span class="dock-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="3"></rect>
        <path d="M10 9l5 3-5 3z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"></path>
      </svg>
    </span>
    <span><%= t("editor.change_animation", default: "Change animation") %></span>
  </button>
  <button type="button" class="dock-btn dock-design"
          data-proxy=".split-left-design-prompt"
          data-action="click->device-frame#proxy"
          title="<%= t("editor.add_design_title", default: "Add an image to this card") %>">
    <span class="dock-icon" aria-hidden="true">＋</span>
    <span><%= t("editor.add_design", default: "Add design") %></span>
  </button>
  <button type="button" class="dock-btn dock-media"
          data-proxy=".add-media-fab"
          data-action="click->device-frame#proxy"
          title="<%= t("editor.change_media_title", default: "Change this card's image") %>">
    <span class="dock-icon" aria-hidden="true">＋</span>
    <span><%= t("editor.change_media", default: "Change media") %></span>
  </button>
  <button type="button" class="dock-btn dock-header-bg"
          data-proxy=".header-bg-fab"
          data-action="click->device-frame#proxy"
          title="<%= t("editor.header_background_title", default: "Colour or image behind this card's animation — the header on a phone") %>">
    <span><%= t("editor.header_background", default: "Header background") %></span>
  </button>
  <button type="button" class="dock-btn dock-reposition"
          data-proxy=".media-adjust-fab"
          data-action="click->device-frame#proxy"
          title="<%= t("editor.reposition_title", default: "Reframe this card's media — drag to reposition, or crop and zoom a photo") %>">
    <span><%= t("editor.reposition", default: "Reposition") %></span>
  </button>
  <button type="button" class="dock-btn dock-mobile-bg"
          data-proxy=".card-bg-fab"
          data-action="click->device-frame#proxy"
          title="<%= t("editor.mobile_background_title", default: "Colour, image or GIF behind this card's question and answers on a phone") %>">
    <span><%= t("editor.mobile_background", default: "Mobile background") %></span>
  </button>
</div>
